<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zaleucus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 7th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zaleucus was the lawgiver of Locri Epizephyrii in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, credited with drawing up the first written Greek law code in the mid-7th century BCE. His laws fixed penalties in advance rather than leaving them to the judges, and were known for their severity. Later stories about him, such as his putting out one of his own eyes to spare his son, are of uncertain value.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zaleucus.jpg" alt="Zaleucus" width="320" height="323" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Published by Guillaume Rouille(1518?-1589) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zaleucus.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
